<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Mancham</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1939–2017</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir James Mancham was a Seychellois politician, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seychelles">Seychelles</a> Democratic Party, who served as chief minister and then as the first president of the Seychelles at independence in 1976. He was overthrown in a coup by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france-albert-rene">France-Albert René</a> in June 1977 while abroad, and lived in exile until his return in 1992.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-mancham.jpg" alt="James Mancham" width="269" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Goverment of Seychelles · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:James_Mancham_-_Official_Portrait_(cropped)_2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
